# Component documentation structure

Every component page in `docs/components/` (excluding `overview.md`) must follow this structural contract.

## Frontmatter dependency

Frontmatter fields and traceability metadata are defined in:

- `frontmatter-contract.mdc`
- `component-figma-traceability.mdc`

## Required sections (in order)

Only these H2 headings are allowed in component pages, in this exact canonical order:

1. `## Overview`
2. `## Anatomy`
3. `## Component API`
4. `## Visual Specifications`
5. `## Variants`
6. `## States`
7. `## Usage Guidelines`
8. `## Content Guidelines`
9. `## Accessibility`
10. `## Related Components`
11. `## Design–Token Discrepancies` (optional, only when real mismatches exist)
12. `## Gaps / TBD` (optional, deterministic binary contract)

No other H2 headings are permitted (`## Examples`, `## Changelog`, etc.).
If additional details are needed, place them under `###` inside the nearest allowed H2.

## `## Gaps / TBD` deterministic contract

- This section is **binary and deterministic**:
  - Include it when unresolved gaps exist in the linked spec.
  - Omit it entirely when no unresolved gaps exist.
- Each item must use checkbox format:
  - `- [ ] [SCHEMA_TBD] ...`
  - `- [ ] [TOKEN_INVALID] ...`
  - `- [ ] [CONTENT_UNKNOWN] ...`
  - `- [ ] [A11Y_TBD] ...`
- Canonical ordering is mandatory:
  1. `SCHEMA_TBD`
  2. `TOKEN_INVALID`
  3. `CONTENT_UNKNOWN`
  4. `A11Y_TBD`

## General rules

- Every required section (1-10) must be present; when data is missing, use `TBD` instead of omitting sections.
- Do not add H2 headings outside the canonical allowed list.
- One component per file. File name matches component name in `snake_case` (for example, `status_bar.md`).

## Content guidance

For section-by-section writing guidance, use `component-doc-content.mdc`.
